  "summary": "Magician Lord is Alpha Denshi's side-scrolling action game, first released for Neo Geo MVS in Japan on 26 April 1990.",
  "body": [
    "Magician Lord is Alpha Denshi's side-scrolling action game, first released for Neo Geo MVS in Japan on 26 April 1990. Elta, a descendant of an earlier magician, crosses Cadacis to recover eight grimoires and prevent a destructive power from returning. Magic shots, platforming and doors into dangerous chambers form the journey. As one of the first Neo Geo arcade releases and an early home-console pack-in, it helped introduce the hardware through large, colourful fantasy scenes. Its central ability lets Elta become a different creature by collecting elemental orbs.",
    "Fire, water and wind orbs combine in pairs to create six transformations. A dragon warrior breathes fire, a water-based form attacks along the ground, and other combinations produce fighters with different projectiles or jumping abilities. Choosing and preserving a form changes how Elta handles the next stretch of the stage. The transformation also expands his health, making it protection as well as another weapon. A useful combination can therefore make an intimidating room more manageable, provided the player can avoid losing it before reaching the next major encounter.",
    "Each stage includes doors leading through trap-filled areas towards a miniboss and the final boss guarding a grimoire. Treasure chests supply points, power-ups and the orbs needed for transformation. Taking damage can reduce Elta's attack power and eventually return him to his ordinary body, so strength remains something to protect. Hideki Yamamoto, Hiroaki Shimizu and Yuka Watanabe composed the score. The colourful forms and imposing enemies gave the early Neo Geo a memorable display, while the demanding route made control of that power central to surviving it."
  ],
  "story_headings": [
    "One of Neo Geo’s first worlds",
    "Two orbs, another body",
    "Power that can be lost"
  ],
